  "description": "Analog master filter: while its switch is ON, tracks 1-12, delay/reverb returns (always, TEST17) and the input go through the analog FX block, whose filter (LP4/LP2/BP2/HP2/NO1/NO2/LPN or THRU), FREQ and RESO follow the master filter (FX AMP and DRIVE stay the kit's). Edits only the audio interrupt's copy of the live values and, after the OS's FX filter CV routine, its resonance CV (RESO 63-127 climbs past the FX filter's own maximum: Polivoks-style); OFF gives the kit's routing back. TEST15: controls on the FX track's SYN page 2 (page 0 made the SYN tab's second page: A FLTR, B TYPE, C FREQ, D RESO, E CMP: MAIN / FX, what master-comp's dynamics act on, F IN: master-comp's input meter, G empty (TEST17: RET removed, the returns always through the filter; id 412 unused); earlier: G RET FLTR / KIT, the delay/reverb returns through the filter or where the kit routes them; TEST15b); FLTR page 2 and AMP page 2 stock. With the delay's return in the FX block the copy's FX AMP DEL is 0 (the OS mutes that send then anyway; its loop guard would cut the delay's reverb send). TRIM is LVL (SYN page 1 H): the output level of the whole chain, always on, applied by master-comp. The FX DRIVE is the kit's (SYN page 1 A; DRV's code removed in TEST15b). Values global in RAM, not saved. MIDI on the FX CONTROL CH: CC 3/9/12/13 and NRPN 1:48-1:51 (FLTR, TYPE, FREQ, RESO) in, and out on knob turns like the stock knobs.",
